  "context": "## Tiger Teams Model and AI Integrity Management Systems\nAI integrity is presented as an operational condition: the transformed system must remain trustworthy while work continues. Governance, evidence and intervention therefore remain connected to the mission boundary.\n\nThe enterprise-function proposal concerns responsibility that persists after implementation. Specify the operating boundary, the specialist authorities, the exception path and the receiving owner. A delivery team can build the mechanisms, but the handover must identify who can maintain and revise them during normal operation.\n\nIn mission-critical transformation, the project ends the moment operational integrity collapses.\n\nThis is the central principle behind the JubAp.Net approach to AI Integrity Management Systems.\n\nIntegrity is not treated as an external compliance layer, a cybersecurity checklist, an ethics policy, a governance dashboard or a post-deployment audit exercise. It is the condition that allows a transformed operation to remain trustworthy while it continues running.\nTags: Business and management 30.00%; AI integrity and security 40.00%; Transformation and operational continuity 30.00%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/tiger-teams-model-and-ai-integrity-management-systems-n1283/\nSource document: https://jubap.net/tiger-teams-model-and-ai-integrity-management-systems/\n\n",
